{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseSubstratePin","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseSubstratePin","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseFromWeights"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_loopMean_ne_two_on_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_loopMean_ne_two_on_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseSubstratePin.lean#L58-L72","doc":"**Hence the D-frame loop mean is never `2` on `[1, 2]`.**\n\nThe exclusion hypothesis, delivered in the form\n`no_weight_function_gives_phase` consumes it. `q ≠ 0` and `q² + 1 ≠ 0`\nare automatic over `ℝ` on this interval and are discharged here rather\nthan pushed onto the caller. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.quartic_neg_on_Icc_one_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.quartic_neg_on_Icc_one_two","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseSubstratePin.lean#L46-L56","doc":"**The quartic `q⁴ - 2q³ - 2q + 1` is strictly negative on `[1, 2]`**,\nan interval containing the substrate pin `q₀ ≈ 1.10998`.\n\nCombined with `zD_loopMean_sub_two_num`, this says `2·z_D - h ≠ 2` at the\npin, so `no_weight_function_gives_phase` applies there and its exclusion\nis not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0}]}